    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d742">

                <pb facs="0856" n="736" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg736"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                    Dudley.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-06-30"><hi rendition="#italic">June 30,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 360.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 1119, of the 17th ultimo, in regard to the case of Chung Dai Yau, a
                    native of Hawaii, of Chinese parentage, claiming American citizenship under the
                    provisions of Section IV of the act of April 30, 1900, entitled “An act to
                    provide a government for the Territory of Hawaii.”</p>
                <p>In reply I have to inform you that as you are satisfied of the truth of the man’s
                    statements you may issue him a passport.</p>
                <p>The question of his admission to territory of the United States is under the
                    jurisdiction of another Department.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herbert H. D.
                    Peirce</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
